TY  - RPRT
AU  - Torul, Orhan
AU  - Oztunali, Oguz
TI  - Intergenerational Educational Mobility in Europe
PY  - 2026
UR  - https://orhantorul.com/research/ieme/
KW  - Intergenerational Mobility
KW  - Education
KW  - Gender
KW  - Equality of Opportunity
KW  - Great Gatsby Curve
KW  - Europe
AB  - We map intergenerational educational mobility across 34 European countries using all eleven waves of the European Social Survey (296,237 individuals born 1940–1985). The paper makes two methodological contributions: ordered logit models with cohort-varying coefficients trace birth-cohort-specific transition probabilities for each country and four groups of countries, and an Oaxaca–Blinder decomposition separates structural from compositional change in aggregate persistence. Group trajectories diverge sharply. Mediterranean persistence falls from 84% to about 40%, a decline that is 93% structural. Nordic persistence follows a U-shape alongside falling persistence among children of low-educated parents. Post-Socialist persistence rises from 44% to 57%, yet the rise is entirely compositional: the net contribution of changes in conditional persistence is close to zero. The early female persistence disadvantage reverses in the Mediterranean and Rest of Europe groups, and tertiary equality of opportunity stagnates near 0.16 in Post-Socialist countries despite rapid tertiary expansion. Educational inequality and persistence are positively correlated across all 34 countries. Excluding the seven Mediterranean countries reverses the sign, but the estimate is statistically imprecise.
ER  - 
